{"type":"frame-snapshot","snapshot":{"callId":"vrtg@666","phase":"after","pageId":"page@fdcd20cb88cd40ca3e5413e74bc9b069","frameId":"frame@b3d8350057ba166c473a57ec88cc64de","frameUrl":"http://127.0.0.1:39347/","doctype":"html","html":["HTML",{"lang":"en"},[[79,22]],["BODY",{},[[79,23]],["MAIN",{"data-latency":"{}","class":"orb-room"},[[79,25]],[[79,92]],[[59,1]],["DIV",{"class":"floating-surface-layer"},["DIV",{"class":"flexlayout__layout"},[[79,126]],[[79,127]],[[79,128]],[[13,9]],[[3,7]],["DIV",{"class":"flexlayout__float_window","style":"left: 16px; top: 72px; width: 328px; height: 440px; position: absolute;"},[[2,6]],["DIV",{"class":"flexlayout__float_window_content"},["DIV",{"class":"flexlayout__layout"},[[2,7]],[[2,28]],["DIV",{"id":"flexlayout-tab-coordinated-goals","role":"tabpanel","aria-labelledby":"flexlayout-tabbutton-coordinated-goals","tabindex":"-1","class":"flexlayout__tab","data-layout-path":"/sublayout3/ts0/t0","style":"left: 0px; top: 26px; width: 316px; height: 378.203px; position: absolute;"},["DIV",{"class":"flexlayout__tab_moveable","style":"overflow: auto;"},["DIV",{"class":"floating-panel-content","aria-label":"Goals"},["SECTION",{"class":"goal-panel","aria-label":"Coordinated goals"},["P",{},"Progress stays saved when you close this window."],["DETAILS",{"class":"goal-create"},["SUMMARY",{},"New goal"],["FORM",{},["LABEL",{"class":"goal-option"},["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"on","__playwright_checked_":"false","type":"checkbox"}],"Question from public sources"],["LABEL",{},"Goal",["TEXTAREA",{"__playwright_value_":"","aria-label":"Goal","maxlength":"8000","placeholder":"Describe the result you want and what must be true when it is finished."}]],["LABEL",{"class":"goal-option"},["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"on","__playwright_checked_":"false","type":"checkbox"}],"Allow public web research for this goal"],["BUTTON",{"type":"submit","disabled":""},"Start coordinated work"]]],[[2,43]],["ARTICLE",{"tabindex":"-1","data-goal-id":"7c31d3ef-f1c3-4094-85b6-7bab80ca81e7","class":"goal-record"},["H3",{},"Where are the Fetch Standard’s tests kept, and where can I see them running against browser engines? Cite the README statements supporting both."],["P",{"class":"goal-state"},"Completed"," · ","completed"],["P",{},"Saved-source identity checks, answer acceptance and full-question coverage passed. Literal citations are checked; factual answer quality is not independently verified."],["SMALL",{},"Updated ","10/29/2026, 6:06:40 PM"],["P",{},"2"," of ","2"," milestones accepted"],["P",{"class":"goal-current-role"},"Coordinator"," · ","completed"],["SECTION",{"class":"research-brief-create","aria-label":"Create a research brief"},["FORM",{},["H4",{},"Create a cited research brief"],["P",{},"The linked goal reuses this accepted answer and saved source copies. A local writing decision creates a short brief, then host checks create PDF and HTML files."],["LABEL",{},"Brief title",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"Fetch test contributor brief","aria-label":"Brief title","maxlength":"120","value":"Fetch test contributor brief"}]],["LABEL",{},"Your notes for the brief",["TEXTAREA",{"__playwright_value_":"Personal handoff for my next Fetch test contribution. These are my own proposed actions and working notes, not instructions or verified claims from the source.\n\nBefore changing anything, I will record the browser and version, a minimal public example, the outcome I expected and what I actually saw. I will remove cookies, authorization headers, account details and private URLs from anything I share.\n\n1. Reopen this brief and follow its original-source link. Compare the saved retrieval time with the current README. If the evidence changed, ask a new focused question instead of editing the accepted copy.\n2. Open the browser-results location from the brief. Write down the engine and platform I inspected. A saved answer is a pointer to evidence, not proof that a bug exists or a test passes.\n3. Search the cited test directory for a related case before proposing another test. Keep the candidate filename, my reason for choosing it and any unresolved question in my own draft.\n4. Separate reproduction from implementation. First describe a small public fixture and expected behavior; then explain the proposed test and the observation it should distinguish.\n5. Read the project's current contribution and review instructions before submitting anything. I have not checked those instructions yet, and this brief does not establish them.\n6. Keep a handoff log of what I tried, which evidence I saved and what remains uncertain. After interruption, inspect saved work and continue deliberately rather than repeating accepted research.\n7. Preserve the PDF and HTML with their recorded hashes and original citations. Ask for missing guidance instead of guessing. My personal checklist is not a source-backed conclusion.","aria-label":"Your notes for the brief","maxlength":"2000","placeholder":"Optional personal notes, kept separately from source evidence."},"Personal handoff for my next Fetch test contribution. These are my own proposed actions and working notes, not instructions or verified claims from the source.\n\nBefore changing anything, I will record the browser and version, a minimal public example, the outcome I expected and what I actually saw. I will remove cookies, authorization headers, account details and private URLs from anything I share.\n\n1. Reopen this brief and follow its original-source link. Compare the saved retrieval time with the current README. If the evidence changed, ask a new focused question instead of editing the accepted copy.\n2. Open the browser-results location from the brief. Write down the engine and platform I inspected. A saved answer is a pointer to evidence, not proof that a bug exists or a test passes.\n3. Search the cited test directory for a related case before proposing another test. Keep the candidate filename, my reason for choosing it and any unresolved question in my own draft.\n4. Separate reproduction from implementation. First describe a small public fixture and expected behavior; then explain the proposed test and the observation it should distinguish.\n5. Read the project's current contribution and review instructions before submitting anything. I have not checked those instructions yet, and this brief does not establish them.\n6. Keep a handoff log of what I tried, which evidence I saved and what remains uncertain. After interruption, inspect saved work and continue deliberately rather than repeating accepted research.\n7. Preserve the PDF and HTML with their recorded hashes and original citations. Ask for missing guidance instead of guessing. My personal checklist is not a source-backed conclusion."]],["SMALL",{},"Your edits are a draft in this browser until you save the linked goal. Notes are not sent to public source hosts."],["DIV",{"class":"goal-actions research-brief-actions"},["BUTTON",{"type":"submit"},"Save and write brief"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Close brief form"]]],["P",{"role":"status","tabindex":"-1"}]],["SECTION",{"class":"goal-sources","aria-label":"Question sources and answer"},["P",{},"Public-source question · Saved copies stay here when the window closes. Continue reuses them. No PDF, website or vault content is sent to source hosts."],["SECTION",{"tabindex":"-1","class":"goal-reading-plan","aria-label":"Saved reading plan","data-reading-id":"40f1ef83-6031-47bd-8d8f-98f7101b25b0"},["STRONG",{},"Reading plan saved before inference"],["P",{},"Automatic question-term matching selects up to two passages and 1,600 text positions from the full saved copies. This may omit relevant text; it is not a complete source review."],["SMALL",{},"1"," selected passages · Saved ","10/29/2026, 6:06:27 PM"," · ","source-passages-v1"],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Reading identity and exact question"],["P",{},"Where are the Fetch Standard’s tests kept, and where can I see them running against browser e