and what must be true when it is finished."}]],["LABEL",{"class":"goal-option"},["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"on","__playwright_checked_":"false","type":"checkbox"}],"Allow public web research for this goal"],["BUTTON",{"type":"submit","disabled":""},"Start coordinated work"]]],["P",{"role":"status"}],["ARTICLE",{"tabindex":"-1","data-goal-id":"a09643e1-9a33-4d6d-b6d5-dc5e87d516bd","class":"goal-record"},["H3",{},"Fetch test contributor brief"],["P",{"class":"goal-state"},"Stopped"," · ","cancelled"],["P",{},"Stopped by you. The goal, verified milestones and evidence are kept."],["SMALL",{},"Updated ","10/29/2026, 6:06:44 PM"],["P",{},"2"," of ","3"," milestones accepted"],["P",{"class":"goal-current-role"},"Coordinator"," · ","cancelled"],["DIV",{"class":"goal-question-link"},["SMALL",{},"Research brief from the parent’s complete accepted answer and checked source copies. The parent is unchanged."],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Open parent question"]],["DIV",{"class":"goal-brief-controls"},["BUTTON",{},"Continue remaining work"],["SMALL",{},"The title, notes and accepted research are saved. Continue reuses saved writing and document evidence. For changed requirements, create another brief from the original question."]],["SECTION",{"class":"research-brief","aria-label":"Research brief"},["H4",{},"Fetch test contributor brief"],["P",{},"Preparing the writing handoff"],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Saved notes and document identity"],["P",{"class":"research-brief-notes"},"Personal handoff for my next Fetch test contribution. These are my own proposed actions and working notes, not instructions or verified claims from the source.\n\nBefore changing anything, I will record the browser and version, a minimal public example, the outcome I expected and what I actually saw. I will remove cookies, authorization headers, account details and private URLs from anything I share.\n\n1. Reopen this brief and follow its original-source link. Compare the saved retrieval time with the current README. If the evidence changed, ask a new focused question instead of editing the accepted copy.\n2. Open the browser-results location from the brief. Write down the engine and platform I inspected. A saved answer is a pointer to evidence, not proof that a bug exists or a test passes.\n3. Search the cited test directory for a related case before proposing another test. Keep the candidate filename, my reason for choosing it and any unresolved question in my own draft.\n4. Separate reproduction from implementation. First describe a small public fixture and expected behavior; then explain the proposed test and the observation it should distinguish.\n5. Read the project's current contribution and review instructions before submitting anything. I have not checked those instructions yet, and this brief does not establish them.\n6. Keep a handoff log of what I tried, which evidence I saved and what remains uncertain. After interruption, inspect saved work and continue deliberately rather than repeating accepted research.\n7. Preserve the PDF and HTML with their recorded hashes and original citations. Ask for missing guidance instead of guessing. My personal checklist is not a source-backed conclusion."],["SMALL",{},"Personal notes are kept separately from source evidence."],["SMALL",{},"Parent question ","7c31d3ef-f1c3-4094-85b6-7bab80ca81e7"],["SMALL",{},"Writing input SHA-256 ","c4dcef62a9624fa2559cc5419f9cad625c60a1747ad6defbee826219851a1455"]],["P",{},"The saved title and notes are kept through interruption. Use Stop goal or Continue remaining work in this goal; accepted source work is reused."]],["SECTION",{"class":"goal-sources","aria-label":"Question sources and answer"},["P",{},"Public-source question · Saved copies stay here when the window closes. Continue reuses them. No PDF, website or vault content is sent to source hosts."],["SECTION",{"tabindex":"-1","class":"goal-reading-plan","aria-label":"Saved reading plan","data-reading-id":"70426cf3-73da-47c6-96e8-34d54e8763e9"},["STRONG",{},"Reading plan saved before inference"],["P",{},"Explicitly selected passages. The answer is limited to these ranges."],["SMALL",{},"1"," selected passages · Saved ","10/29/2026, 6:06:43 PM"," · ","source-passages-v1"],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Reading identity and exact question"],["P",{},"Where are the Fetch Standard’s tests kept, and where can I see them running against browser engines? Cite the README statements supporting both."],["SMALL",{},"Question SHA-256: ","6f22c7ec184e33bc4ad15bcec90d99181c8ee3314f1e641fc8b70f82f7ffbc1f"],["SMALL",{},"Reading ","70426cf3-73da-47c6-96e8-34d54e8763e9"," · milestone ","source-answer"]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"goal-reading-history"},["SUMMARY",{},"Reading plan history"],["P",{},"Earlier exact questions and passage identities stay saved. History loads only when opened; inspecting a plan reads its verified saved ranges."],["DIV",{"class":"goal-actions"}]],["ARTICLE",{"class":"goal-source","aria-label":"Saved source source-1"},["STRONG",{},"[","source-1","] ","README.md"],["A",{"href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/whatwg/fetch/main/README.md","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer"},"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/whatwg/fetch/main/README.md"],["SMALL",{},"Retrieved ","10/29/2026, 6:06:27 PM"," · ","text/plain"," · ","4,815"," response bytes · ","4,815"," text positions"],["SMALL",{},"Copied from snapshot ","9cf16e8d-e92f-4b15-9b57-f68e2fc0490e"," in question ","7c31d3ef-f1c3-4094-85b6-7bab80ca81e7",", without a new public fetch."],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Content identity"],["SMALL",{},"Response SHA-256: ","d484144421db3f758ef98fe5bf13c3dbe1e07a357033af5288298ea0f4f2ceaa"],["SMALL",{},"Text SHA-256: ","d484144421db3f758ef98fe5bf13c3dbe1e07a357033af5288298ea0f4f2ceaa"],["SMALL",{},"Snapshot ","52d48f68-3ab1-467d-bbd4-f5467e4b41ef"," · ","public-text-v1",". Text positions use UTF-16 offsets. Acquisition checks do not establish factual accuracy."]],["OL",{"class":"goal-source-ranges"},