URL labels use the target. Facts, citation IDs and literal source quotes are not rewritten."],["SMALL",{},"brief-inline-v1"],["SMALL",{},"Presented wording SHA-256 ","68a38029a44502c9ba9aadcb179d8d2c54466f826cc3cbf7e535a84c37ae6aed"],["SMALL",{},"The original native wording and decision remain in the writing inspection below."]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Saved notes and document identity"],["P",{"class":"research-brief-notes"},"Personal handoff for my next Fetch test contribution. These are my own proposed actions and working notes, not instructions or verified claims from the source.\n\nBefore changing anything, I will record the browser and version, a minimal public example, the outcome I expected and what I actually saw. I will remove cookies, authorization headers, account details and private URLs from anything I share.\n\n1. Reopen this brief and follow its original-source link. Compare the saved retrieval time with the current README. If the evidence changed, ask a new focused question instead of editing the accepted copy.\n2. Open the browser-results location from the brief. Write down the engine and platform I inspected. A saved answer is a pointer to evidence, not proof that a bug exists or a test passes.\n3. Search the cited test directory for a related case before proposing another test. Keep the candidate filename, my reason for choosing it and any unresolved question in my own draft.\n4. Separate reproduction from implementation. First describe a small public fixture and expected behavior; then explain the proposed test and the observation it should distinguish.\n5. Read the project's current contribution and review instructions before submitting anything. I have not checked those instructions yet, and this brief does not establish them.\n6. Keep a handoff log of what I tried, which evidence I saved and what remains uncertain. After interruption, inspect saved work and continue deliberately rather than repeating accepted research.\n7. Preserve the PDF and HTML with their recorded hashes and original citations. Ask for missing guidance instead of guessing. My personal checklist is not a source-backed conclusion."],["SMALL",{},"Personal notes are kept separately from source evidence."],["SMALL",{},"Parent question ","7c31d3ef-f1c3-4094-85b6-7bab80ca81e7"],["SMALL",{},"Writing input SHA-256 ","c4dcef62a9624fa2559cc5419f9cad625c60a1747ad6defbee826219851a1455"],["SMALL",{},"Native draft SHA-256 ","e67e669138de250604ba002fdb8cec0a9caf20b0243b47e87c3fd6f392a46e88"]],["DETAILS",{"class":"research-brief-writing"},["SUMMARY",{},"Saved native writing and support review"],["P",{},"Host content check passed: ","Host checked one plain-prose paragraph, citation selections and absence of introduced URLs or host-provenance claims. Semantic support still requires the separate native review."],["SMALL",{},"Original native wording before host presentation:"],["P",{},"The Fetch Standard’s tests are kept in the `fetch/` directory of `web-platform-tests/wpt` and can be seen at [wpt.fyi/results/fetch](https://wpt.fyi/results/fetch)."," ","[1] [2]"],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Original native writing decision"],["SMALL",{},"Writing decision SHA-256 ","e67e669138de250604ba002fdb8cec0a9caf20b0243b47e87c3fd6f392a46e88"],["PRE",{"tabindex":"0","aria-label":"Original native writing decision JSON","style":"max-height: 240px; overflow: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere;"},"{\n  \"paragraphs\": [\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Fetch Standard’s tests are kept in the `fetch/` directory of `web-platform-tests/wpt` and can be seen at [wpt.fyi/results/fetch](https://wpt.fyi/results/fetch).\",\n      \"citations\": [\n        1,\n        2\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}"]],["SMALL",{},"Model support checks do not independently verify source claims. The source copies and literal citations remain inspectable below."]],["P",{},"The saved title and notes are kept through interruption. Use Stop goal or Continue remaining work in this goal; a