,["BR"],["BR"],"1. Reopen this brief and follow its original-source link. Compare the saved retrieval time with the current README. If the evidence changed, ask a new focused question instead of editing the accepted copy.",["BR"],"2. Open the browser-results location from the brief. Write down the engine and platform I inspected. A saved answer is a pointer to evidence, not proof that a bug exists or a test passes.",["BR"],"3. Search the cited test directory for a related case before proposing another test. Keep the candidate filename, my reason for choosing it and any unresolved question in my own draft.",["BR"],"4. Separate reproduction from implementation. First describe a small public fixture and expected behavior; then explain the proposed test and the observation it should distinguish.",["BR"],"5. Read the project's current contribution and review instructions before submitting anything. I have not checked those instructions yet, and this brief does not establish them.",["BR"],"6. Keep a handoff log of what I tried, which evidence I saved and what remains uncertain. After interruption, inspect saved work and continue deliberately rather than repeating accepted research.",["BR"],"7. Preserve the PDF and HTML with their recorded hashes and original citations. Ask for missing guidance instead of guessing. My personal checklist is not a source-backed conclusion."],"\n",["P",{},"Reference [1] · Literal saved-source quote (source-1, text 1914–2055): Tests for the Fetch Standard can be found in the `fetch/` directory of [`web-platform-tests/wpt`](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt)."],"\n",["P",{},"Reference [2] · Literal saved-source quote (source-1, text 2057–2189): A dashboard showing the tests running against browser engines can be seen at [wpt.fyi/results/fetch](https://wpt.fyi/results/fetch)."],"\n",["H2",{},"Saved source source-1"],["P",{},"README.md"],"\n",["P",{},"URL: ",["A",{"href":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/whatwg/fetch/main/README.md","rel